Package: bad-pdf
Version: 1.1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Alienkrishn [Anon4You]
Depends: curl, python, termux-tools
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/deepzec/Bad-Pdf
Description: Create malicious PDFs to steal NTLM hashes from Windows
 Bad-PDF generates PDF files that exploit a Checkpoint‑disclosed
 vulnerability to force NTLM (NTLMv1/NTLMv2) authentication attempts
 from Windows machines. Works on all PDF readers and often evades
 EDR/endpoint solutions. Use with Responder to capture the hashes
 for authorised security testing.
